	(text "TWO-PHASE CLOCK: PH1 = NOR(CLK, PH2) opens the masters while CLK is low, PH2 = NOR(CLKN, PH1) opens the slaves while CLK is high.  The cross-coupling means a phase cannot start rising until the other is fully low, whatever the threshold spread between transistors, so a flip-flop is never transparent.  CLK from the header has one load here."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 165.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5525c734-8ae4-475f-ac46-862aadc24bb8")
	)
